Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] feat(android): tell the app when its picture in picture
 gives way to another device of ours

Android's picture in picture is the app's own (it runs the activity's), so the
rule iOS's system picture in picture follows (patch 5: the same person in the
call on another device with its camera on; a main device never gives way to a
second-device ticket) reaches it as an event: with the feature flag
android.pip-give-way.enabled the SDK sends PICTURE_IN_PICTURE_GIVE_WAY_CHANGED
(givesWay: boolean) whenever that changes in a conference. The app then doesn't
go to picture in picture as it leaves, and leaves it if it's showing, which
also lets the camera go off in the background as Jitsi's does.

One rule for both platforms, decided where the presence identities are (the
app's web view knows nothing of them). Without the flag nothing is sent.
